Kamakura Prefecture, Kamakura Prefecture

13
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:50,900
Let it rain

14
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:55,020
Everybody can do, I started running

15
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,240
Dreams never stop, you know

16
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,480
Let's set sail again tomorrow

17
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,260
Let it rain

18
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:07,680
Everybody can do, just a little

19
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,860
Even if we stick out, it doesn't hurt

20
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:15,000
Don't make a fuss, don't attack

21
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:17,240
Stronger, higher

22
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:31,680
Men's bonding, Kinoki Buro

23
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:40,140
So cool!

24
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:42,240
It's the Mugatti Ryotsu Special!

25
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:44,560
It's not just fast, you know.

26
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,020
Just watch.

27
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:47,300
It won't go.

28
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:48,900
Whoa!

29
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:52,600
Outstanding cornering performance.

30
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,800
Wow, that's amazing!

31
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:57,040
Disc brakes fitted

32
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:58,500
Lights on too

33
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,240
Four-wheel independent suspension

34
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:01,540
Three-speed transmission

35
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,100
Twin-motor system

36
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:04,620
Modified at a cost of 100,000 yen

37
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:06,240
It's my masterpiece

38
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,160
I'm amazing too,

39
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:11,160
but my driving technique is incredible too!

40
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:12,920
Wow!

41
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:15,380
Whoa, Ryo-san, you're something else!

42
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:17,900
So cool!

43
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:18,340
What?

44
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:20,880
This one's even more incredible!

45
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,260
Go, Super Jan!

46
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:26,360
Hey, don't get too carried away!

47
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,920
It's the Chief's fault!

48
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,460
You just suddenly popped
up in a place like that!

49
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:41,520
The Bugatti's not broken at all.

50
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,800
Because I reinforced the frame.

51
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:46,220
It won't break just from hitting a person.

52
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:47,520
Ryotsu!

53
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,420
Yes, what is it, Chief?

54
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:52,920
Where am I?

55
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:56,460
Chief Ohara,
you're not old enough to be senile yet.

56
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:58,900
Obviously you're inside the police box.

57
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:03,620
Did you lose your memory from the
shock of selling your balls or something?

58
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:06,580
It's me, it's Ryotsu!

59
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:08,740
Do you remember me?

60
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,140
You idiot!

61
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:17,040
Ryotsu!
What is this police box supposed to be?

62
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,760
Is it a children's playground?

63
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,140
Or a racing course for
radio-controlled cars?

64
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,220
Of course not!

65
00:03:22,460 --> 00:03:25,420
It's the sacred workplace
of us police officers!

66
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:29,740
You don't have to yell like that. We
understand what the Chief is trying to say!

67
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:32,480
The Chief doesn't have amnesia!

68
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:33,940
You don't understand at all!

69
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:37,500
I've had enough, once and for all today.

70
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:39,360
Effective from this moment,

71
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:43,480
all personal items unrelated to work
are strictly banned from being brought in.

72
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:45,820
It's a personal item ban!

73
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,960
What an unbelievable guy.

74
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:58,840
I didn't realize you'd brought
in this many personal belongings.

75
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:03,140
There's still this much left
that won't fit in one load.

76
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:06,200
We'll need at least three more trips.

77
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:07,620
Listen.

78
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:11,100
Once you've put yours in your room,
come right back, you hear?

79
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,200
I know.

80
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:19,540
You can't even tell a
workplace from a playground.

81
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:20,620
That guy...

82
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:23,700
So it's this one.

83
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:26,160
The one who bumped into me just now...

84
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,340
I'd like to smash it to pieces.

85
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:31,400
I heard that one costs 100,000 yen.

86
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,040
What?

87
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:34,320
100,000 yen!

88
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:39,180
I can't understand someone who spends
100,000 yen on something like this.

89
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,940
What's this one?

90
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,740
A radio, maybe?

91
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:48,360
Can't you hear it?

92
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:50,680
I can't figure out the switch.

93
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:58,380
Terai, is it really 100,000 yen?

94
00:04:58,780 --> 00:04:59,960
Yes, probably.

95
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:01,660
It's in there.

96
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:04,740
It's gone out onto the road!

97
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:08,740
We have to stop it quickly,
or a car will come!

98
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:11,100
How do you make it stop?

99
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,880
It's gotten faster.

100
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:16,120
Hurry up and switch it over!

101
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:17,940
I can't do that!

102
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,440
A car's coming!

103
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:22,160
Uh-oh.

104
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:26,700
Don't stop right there!

105
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,400
That was close.

106
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,360
They're coming from the other side too!

107
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:38,280
I can't stay calm.

108
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:41,560
My life is about to be cut short.

109
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:47,060
I'm starting to figure it out.

110
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:51,020
Chief, now it's a duck from the right!

111
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:53,060
Alright, evacuate to the opposite lane!

112
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:55,620
Nice.

113
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:57,080
We're safe now.

114
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,140
We weren't hit.

115
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:04,980
Scared the hell out of me.

116
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,660
Alright, let's grab it while we can.

117
00:06:07,660 --> 00:06:08,140
Right.

118
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:19,280
Even if they're fine
after bumping into someone,

119
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,100
in front of a tire roller,

120
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,820
they wouldn't stand a chance

121
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:28,680
What do we do?
He's going to be furious, for sure.

122
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:38,160
That was awfully quick.

123
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:40,640
You're the one who told us to
come back right away, Chief.

124
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,220
There's still some left, after all.

125
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:43,920
Right.

126
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,440
Getting old, my memory's getting terrible.

127
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:50,980
Where did the Bugatti go?

128
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:52,440
Chief

129
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,200
Didn't you see my remote-control car?

130
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:58,500
The remote-control car that crashed into the Chief,
you mean.

131
00:06:59,100 --> 00:06:59,900
R-right.

132
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:02,100
I was sure I left it right here.

133
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:06,300
Now that you mention it,
those kids from earlier borrowed it.

134
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,740
That's right.

135
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:10,760
You lent it out without permission?

136
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:14,000
That's strange.

137
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,800
I ran into Junpei and the others
on the way back here, though.

138
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:22,220
Now that I think about it,
was it different kids?

139
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:24,940
After all, you know so many people.

140
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:26,600
Chief.

141
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:30,260
Did you really lend it to the kids?

142
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:32,200
Of course I did.

143
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,480
Why would I lie?

144
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:36,900
Really?

145
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:41,060
I'm not lying.

146
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:42,720
Then why are you looking away?

147
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:44,580
If you're not lying,

148
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:46,740
you should be able to look
me straight in the eye.

149
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,140
Of course I can!

150
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:55,760
Whoever asks loses.

151
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:10,000
You're definitely hiding something, aren't you?
Why is my radio controller here?

152
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:16,240
Could it be...

153
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:18,960
my Bugatti Ryotsu Special?

154
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,440
Chief Ohara moved it

155
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:24,820
and the tire roller ran over it.

156
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:25,980
Big mouth.

157
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:26,920
Chief.

158
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:31,760
It's your fault to begin with.

159
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:34,120
Bringing stuff like
that into the police box.

160
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,160
And then breaking it.

161
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:36,400
That's not fair.

162
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:39,200
I'm a victim here too!

163
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,160
I got hit by something too.

164
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:44,160
So you're saying it's fine to break
my treasure just because of that?

165
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:47,880
I'm sorry about that matter,

166
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:52,760
but in the end,
your bad conduct is what led to this result.

167
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,520
Be more careful from now on.

168
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:57,020
What a way to talk!

169
00:08:57,020 --> 00:09:01,060
Even if you kowtow, lick my feet, and
cry while apologizing, I won't forgive you.

170
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:05,580
If it means licking your feet,
then I'd rather you not forgive me.

171
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:09,960
Now, now, you two are acting like children.

172
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:10,800
Shut up!

173
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:13,780
This...

174
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:18,840
So that's what happened.

175
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:19,440
This...

176
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:21,980
Don't go down yet!

177
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:24,900
I'm getting my revenge for today,
no matter what.

178
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:27,960
The Chief has it rough too

179
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:29,220
Yeah, exactly.

180
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:32,360
Speaking of which,
Chief Ohara's in the book.

181
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,200
I was going to show it to you, senpai.

182
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:48,120
This is the
"Chief's Treasure" corner. The treasure of Chief Ohara of the Kameari Kōen-mae police box is the hinoki bath he just had remodeled.

183
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:55,560
Soaking in the hinoki bath at the end of the day blows away all my fatigue.
It's truly like being in heaven.

184
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:59,580
You've really done it now,
wrecking my treasure!

185
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:01,560
What's this "Hinagi Blockway"!

186
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:02,520
Aah

187
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,200
Hey, get out of the way and look!

188
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:06,260
It's because you went
bragging about your bath!

189
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,180
Wait a minute.

190
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:11,340
A bath is your treasure, is it?

191
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,620
Hehehe.

192
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:15,540
This is fine, right?

193
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:17,480
An assortment of bath salts, right?

194
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,580
Why would you go to the trouble
of buying something like this?

195
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:23,800
I'm giving it to the Chief as a present.

196
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:25,240
But...

197
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:29,100
Just swap out the contents.

198
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:35,580
Into a special bath salt, see? Grind up
chili powder, pepper seeds, and so on.

199
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:42,080
This improves circulation.
Honda, have a little taste. Me?

200
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:45,960
Just a spoonful. Don't argue!

201
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,320
Haa!

202
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:50,180
Aaaaaah!

203
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:57,400
If you put this in a bath,
you'll die of shock!

204
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:59,460
Don't be so dramatic.

205
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:00,300
This stuff?

206
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,940
It might actually kill someone from shock.

207
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:07,940
Let's add some powdered
milk to make it milder.

208
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:10,980
Mix this into the frozen sugar,

209
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:13,300
and if you seal it up
tight again like before,

210
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:14,940
there, done.

211
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:16,740
Special bath salts, complete!

212
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:19,320
Let's call it "Super Spicy Sugar."

213
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:23,580
It's a shame we won't
get to see the Chief panic.

214
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:27,880
Next, the second batch.

215
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:30,300
Rat droppings and sparrow droppings,

216
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:34,060
plus chicken droppings and goldfish droppings,
and it's complete.

217
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:36,740
Where did I even collect all this from?

218
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,340
Renamed "Scent of the Demon,"

219
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:39,780
"Scent of the Kozue-eye."

220
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:40,860
That's pretty intense.

221
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:44,860
Next, miso soup, ochazuke, and consommé.

222
00:11:44,860 --> 00:11:47,340
This should make a nice broth for the Chief.

223
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:49,860
What should I mix in next?

224
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:54,960
Right, more potency from
the serpentine carrot extract.

225
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:57,400
Mixing these things is getting fun.

226
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,320
I'm starting to get scared.

227
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:03,020
And finally,
the ultimate special bath salts.

228
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:07,700
This plaster is specially mixed,
so it hardens fast.

229
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,700
By the time you notice, it's rock-solid.

230
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,880
The Chief's shoulder will come off

231
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:16,480
We can make a life-size doll.

232
00:12:17,020 --> 00:12:19,260
If I do say so myself,
it's a wonderful gift.

233
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:23,180
I'll send this to the
Chief's house by courier.

234
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:24,400
Wait.

235
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,920
If it's from my name, he'll be suspicious.

236
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:29,520
Let's send it under
the station chief's name.

237
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:31,260
You're devious, aren't you.

238
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:34,440
Chief, enjoy it to the fullest.

239
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:37,720
A hinoki bath with the special bath salts.

240
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,440
Chief Ohara

241
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,440
Reiko told Nakagawa

242
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:04,700
You're still bothered about it?

243
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:07,020
that you broke Ryo-chan's
remote-control car,

244
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,080
Whatever the reason,

245
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:14,400
you did break something that cost 100,000 yen,
so it's a fact.

246
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:17,740
Ever since then,
Ryo-chan won't even speak to me.

247
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:21,180
It seems I've completely
missed my chance to make up.

248
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:22,620
That's a real problem.

249
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,520
Well, I have a good idea.

250
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:31,100
What? You're treating me to dinner?

251
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:33,640
Reiko and Nakagawa are treating me?

252
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:37,360
Yes, we wanted to thank you
for always looking after us.

253
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:40,800
Well, well,
what exactly are you treating me to?

254
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,640
That's a surprise until we get there.

255
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,740
Kei-chan should be coming to
pick us up in the car soon.

256
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,520
Take me anywhere.

257
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:51,840
About now, at the Chief's house,

258
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:54,880
the special bath salts should be arriving.

259
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,940
Looks like it's going
to be the best day ever.

260
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:57,820
Ryo-chan, we're here.

261
00:13:57,820 --> 00:13:59,700
Sorry to keep you waiting.

262
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,440
Good work.

263
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:05,760
A limousine pickup? How lavish.

264
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:09,260
There's alcohol, a TV,
karaoke, and games too.

265
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:10,160
Let's see, let's see.

266
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:12,140
Yahoo!

267
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:18,020
My hopes for dinner keep growing.

268
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:23,040
We're here, senpai.

269
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:30,880
Well, I wonder what they'll be feeding us.

270
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:36,060
This view has nothing to
do with fancy restaurants.

271
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:38,480
Could this be...

272
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:41,000
The Chief's house, damn it!

273
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:44,560
Chief Ohara wants to make up with Ryo-chan.

274
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:46,620
Hey -

275
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:47,900
Let's go, Nakagawa.

276
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:49,760
Wait, Ryo-chan!

277
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,220
I don't like that attitude of
trying to win me over with food.

278
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:57,380
I suffered a hundred thousand yen in damages,
you know!

279
00:14:57,380 --> 00:15:01,080
But the Chief's waiting, and they've
gone to the trouble of preparing a feast.

280
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:03,660
The Chief's feast can't be much.

281
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:06,020
At best, it'll be sashimi or tonkatsu.

282
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:09,040
People of that generation are too cheap and shabby.
It's unacceptable.

283
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,640
Sorry for being cheap and shabby

284
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,260
Aaaaaaah!

285
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:19,640
Showing up from far away in that black limo,
scaring the daylights out of me!

286
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:24,640
Ryotsu: About the other day, I...

287
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:31,620
Sorry, sorry, sorry...
I've seen a slim sumo wrestler!

288
00:15:31,620 --> 00:15:36,740
Well, it's awkward standing out here.
Everyone, come in.

289
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:37,760
Yes.

290
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:39,300
Let's do that, then.

291
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:41,120
Weren't you supposed to apologize?

292
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:42,460
He's just embarrassed.

293
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,740
Isn't Hiromi here?

294
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:47,240
She went on a ski trip with friends,
you know.

295
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,900
Now I really want to go home.

296
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:53,780
Just as I expected.

297
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:57,160
Come on, come on, let's go all out tonight!

298
00:15:57,680 --> 00:15:59,400
You like sashimi and tonkatsu, right?

299
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:01,880
I prepared plenty today, Ryotsu.

300
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:06,400
This sashimi is frozen, isn't it?

301
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:11,280
The stuff you bought on sale at the supermarket three days ago,
I put it in the fridge, didn't I?

302
00:16:14,300 --> 00:16:17,740
And this tonkatsu is made from cheap cuts of meat,
from the tendon part.

303
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:20,820
The other dishes are all made
from cheap ingredients too.

304
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:25,660
Even counting the sake,
I'd say it's about 850 yen per person.

305
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:27,000
Sharp one, aren't you.

306
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:32,760
You smashed something worth 100,000 yen, so if it only costs
850 yen to make up for it, that's cheap, isn't it, Chief?

307
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:37,480
I don't think this meal is meant to replace the remote-control car,
or anything.

308
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:43,280
I do intend to pay you back
properly once my bonus comes through.

309
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:44,960
Really.

310
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:50,380
Today is, well, a down payment,
or rather an apology, you see.

311
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,160
That's why I invited you to dinner.

312
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:55,400
If that's the case,
you should have said so earlier, Chief!

313
00:16:57,440 --> 00:17:01,400
So looking closely,
how delicious it all looks!

314
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:04,200
My tonkatsu!

315
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:06,133
No, well,

316
00:17:06,183 --> 00:17:10,140
So even cheap ingredients can taste this good,
depending on how you cook them.

317
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:14,960
Hey, don't eat mine, eat your own!

318
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,880
Looks like you two have made up,
at least for now.

319
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:18,340
Yeah.

320
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:20,480
Cheers!

321
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:25,660
That's right, Chief.

322
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,820
You switched to a hinoki bath, didn't you?
May we see it?

323
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:33,780
Sure. You can use it anytime,
24 hours a day.

324
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:35,880
Reiko-kun, you should go in too.

325
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,720
Yes, thank you.

326
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:39,280
Come on, come on, Chief.

327
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,580
Sorry about that.

328
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:42,900
A bath? Sounds nice.

329
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:45,600
A bath?

330
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,720
C-Chief...

331
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:53,520
Chief, do you use bath salts in your bath?

332
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:57,340
I usually do,
but unfortunately I've run out.

333
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:00,320
I see. That's a shame.

334
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:04,940
Looks like my special bath
salts haven't arrived yet.

335
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:07,940
You should go in later too.

336
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:09,440
Yes, thank you.

337
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:16,940
Feeling great.

338
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:20,160
Tonight is really fun.

339
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,460
It's been ages since I
had a banquet this lively.

340
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:24,891
Ryotsu,

341
00:18:24,941 --> 00:18:28,729
I really feel bad for what I did to you.

342
00:18:28,779 --> 00:18:30,420
Please forgive me.

343
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:33,382
Understood. Let's get in the bath together,

344
00:18:33,432 --> 00:18:36,560
and wash everything away with the grime.

345
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:39,720
Alright, I'll wash your back for you.

346
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:43,700
That was a really lovely bath.

347
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:46,880
Is that so? Then we're going too.

348
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:48,860
I'm looking forward to it.

349
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:52,780
Reiko, will you join us in the bath too?

350
00:18:52,780 --> 00:18:54,520
I don't mind at all.

351
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:56,980
The Chief's unusually drunk, isn't he?

352
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,600
Who could that be at this hour?

353
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:02,980
Ryotsu, go on in ahead.

354
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:03,580
Coming, coming.

355
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:05,280
I'm opening it now.

356
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:11,540
Not bad for a stingy Chief,
he built himself a pretty nice bath.

357
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:14,000
The water's just the right temperature.

358
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:14,960
Here you go, Ryotsu.

359
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:15,939
Ryotsu,

360
00:19:15,989 --> 00:19:19,900
Bath salts arrived by
courier from the Chief!

361
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:20,980
Whoa!

362
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:26,120
My special bath salts!

363
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:28,900
Perfect timing, let's use them right away.

364
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:30,520
Where are you going?

365
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:33,560
U-uh, I just remembered some
business I have to take care of.

366
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:36,760
You've got time for a bath, surely.

367
00:19:36,760 --> 00:19:40,100
Actually, I'm allergic to hinoki baths.

368
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:43,280
Nice joke, Ryotsu.

369
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:50,520
Your old man's still alive, isn't he?

370
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:53,200
Come on, we promised to bathe together,
didn't we?

371
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:54,560
No let's, l-let's, l-let's, l-let's.

372
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:56,780
There are so many to choose from,
I can't decide.

373
00:19:58,760 --> 00:19:59,940
Alright, I'll go with this one.

374
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:01,880
Forest scent.

375
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:03,440
Ooh, the scent of a carp pond.

376
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,880
Stir it well, and...

377
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:10,020
Ugh, it stinks!

378
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:12,720
Wow, what a lovely scent!

379
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:14,900
Because he's drunk,

380
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:16,420
he hasn't noticed at all.

381
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:19,960
Hinoki baths really are the best,
aren't they?

382
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:20,880
Yes, they are.

383
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:23,760
Hinoki is the best wood for a bath,
after all.

384
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:25,880
This feels good.

385
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:27,260
Refreshing.

386
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:28,720
Go on, you first.

387
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:31,820
Hey, should I get out without
even getting in the tub?

388
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:35,080
Please stop, Chief.

389
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:37,460
Wrestling with another man

390
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:40,580
taking a bath together

391
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:43,120
was supposed to wash everything away in the hot water,
remember?

392
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:47,960
Fine, I'll get in.
Happy now? I'm getting in.

393
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:50,500
Make sure you soak up to your shoulders.

394
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:53,440
Why does this have to happen to me?

395
00:20:53,700 --> 00:20:54,840
Get in further.

396
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:57,800
Extra-spicy sugar.

397
00:20:58,340 --> 00:21:00,040
No, that's not allowed.
If you put that in...

398
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,480
I said soak up to your shoulders.

399
00:21:04,540 --> 00:21:05,340
What's wrong?

400
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:10,140
My mucous membranes.
My blood's been bad lately.

401
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:13,880
I thought my whole body was going to go
"hee-hee-hee!" from the shock.

402
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:16,900
Sorry about that.

403
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:19,220
It's no trouble at all.

404
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:21,460
I'll bury it now, while I can.

405
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:24,380
Alright, now I'll wash you down.

406
00:21:24,380 --> 00:21:25,880
No, I'm fine.

407
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:28,200
Are you not going to let me wash you?

408
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:30,940
Fine, fine, I'll let you. Please.

409
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:34,500
Well, I'm very good at washing, you know.

410
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:35,080
Yeah, yeah.

411
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:41,400
No stain stands a chance
once it's in my hands...

412
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,380
Ugh...

413
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:16,720
I told you I'm allergic! If you're allergic too,
let's get in together, Ryo-san.

414
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:19,780
Let's have a naked bonding session between men,
shall we?

415
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:27,020
This is hell, Chief. Being squeezed
together in such a big bath...

416
00:22:27,020 --> 00:22:30,400
Can't we get some distance?
...Yeah, fair enough.

417
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:35,200
Well, should I add a little more bath salt?

418
00:22:38,760 --> 00:22:39,800
That's not allowed!

419
00:22:42,540 --> 00:22:43,420
Uh-oh.

420
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:46,120
We have to get out of here quickly.

421
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:50,700
You just got in!

422
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:53,160
Do you really hate getting
in separately that much?

423
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:55,340
It's not that!

424
00:22:55,340 --> 00:22:57,360
We really have to get out now,
it's seriously bad.

425
00:22:57,360 --> 00:22:58,820
What's bad about it?

426
00:22:58,820 --> 00:23:01,160
The bath salt I just put in was plaster!

427
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:03,460
Why is the bath salt plaster?

428
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:08,280
I feel like my body's getting heavy somehow.

429
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:10,040
It's started to harden.

430
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:12,200
That's why I've been
telling you it's plaster!

431
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:13,560
Get out quick!

432
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:14,200
Hold on a minute.

433
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:18,500
How did you know this bath salt was plaster?

434
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:23,020
You've been scheming something nasty again,
haven't you!

435
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:25,840
Never mind that, get out quick!

436
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:27,620
What was that voice just now?

437
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:29,600
It sounded like Ryo-chan's voice...

438
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:31,960
Somebody help me!

439
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:32,920
It's the bathroom!

440
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:37,000
Nakagawa, help me!

441
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,720
My body won't move.

442
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:41,580
What were you thinking,
making something like this?

443
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:42,960
You complete idiot!

444
00:23:42,960 --> 00:23:46,720
This all started because you
broke the radio control tube, Chief.

445
00:23:47,220 --> 00:23:49,500
You're still going to say that?

446
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:53,600
Looks like we're back
to square one after all.

447
00:23:54,140 --> 00:23:55,780
Honestly, you're hopeless.

448
00:23:58,060 --> 00:23:59,640
It's plaster...

449
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:00,960
It's setting.

450
00:24:04,620 --> 00:24:06,780
S-security for the Hina Festival?

451
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:09,060
Give me a break, Chief.

452
00:24:09,060 --> 00:24:12,920
Ever since I was born, March 3rd
has never brought me anything good.

453
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:13,980
It's a condiment.

454
00:24:13,980 --> 00:24:17,880
Of all things, I hate the Hina
Festival and tsukudani the most.

455
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:21,280
Next time, we'll have plenty of Hina Festival,
so take care of it.

456
00:24:28,980 --> 00:24:32,700
Even if you stop the clock,

457
00:24:34,460 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps passing by.

458
00:24:39,320 --> 00:24:42,700
Don't keep that sour face,

459
00:24:44,360 --> 00:24:48,000
laugh it off and keep on living.

460
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:57,920
Even if today it's raining,

461
00:24:57,920 --> 00:25:03,460
tomorrow will be sunny.

462
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye,

463
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,900
bad things, farewell.

464
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:21,480
Oh yeah, let's live the way we like.

465
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:24,000
Good things will come.

466
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:30,280
Outside the door, the sun is calling you.

467
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

